# Anthropic — Effective context engineering for AI agents

URL: https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/effective-context-engineering-for-ai-agents
Published: September 29, 2025. Rechecked September 5, 2026.

Primary engineering description. Context is input available to the language model during generation, including externally retrieved information. Tools can pull new context into a run. Its note-taking section describes externally stored notes being read back into later context; this is not a claim that a model is retrained by merely reading a note. No product limits, universal memory architecture or complete incident explanation is inherited.

Exact excerpts:
> Context refers to the set of tokens
> LLMs autonomously using tools in a loop.

This source supports the general mechanism, not attribution or causes of the wiki incident.


